  "body": "## Cause\n\nPR #3159 (f036dddad) added \"Router ball nose 6 mm\" to `assets/tools/catalog.json` before \"BN-0600\". `tool_gate::catalog_suggestion` selects the entry nearest 6 mm, then the smaller size. A full tie kept the first entry in file order. Thus the refusal for a ball-nose operation named 'Router ball nose 6 mm', and `the_refusal_names_a_fitting_catalog_entry` (which expects 'BN-0600') failed on main. PR #3139 has no part in the failure.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `crates/app/src/operation/tool_gate.rs`: when the size is a full tie, the entry with the lower name wins (`then_with(|| na.cmp(nb))`). This is a deterministic rule, not a preference for one tool line. The hint does not change when the catalog file order changes. The taper kind had the same risk (\"Router V-bit 60/90 deg 6 mm\" come before \"CM-0600-90\"), and the rule covers it.\n- New pin `a_size_tie_picks_by_name_not_file_order` in `crates/app/tests/tool_gate.rs`:\n  - the pair \"Router ball nose 6 mm\" / \"BN-0600\" in the two file orders gives 'BN-0600';\n  - the full catalog and the reversed catalog give 'BN-0600' (ball-nose), 'EM-0600-4FL' (end mill) and 'CM-0600-90' (taper).\n- The assert of `the_refusal_names_a_fitting_catalog_entry` does not change.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/3170-catalog-hint-tie-by-name.md`.\n\n## Readings (own worktree, head 3f945362a, CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=12, -j 12)\n\n- `cargo xtask gate test the_refusal_names_a_fitting_catalog_entry --crate app --binary tool_gate --exact`: ok.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test tool_gate`: 10 passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test tool_library`: 15 passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --dry-run` says that the diff reaches the 199 `app` heavy lanes (each `app` change reaches them). They did not run. The change touches only the text of a refusal hint, not a toolpath or posted output. The PR is not ready until the reached heavy lanes run on the final head, or the coordinator decides otherwise.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: medium (issue label effort:low; no escalation)\n\nFixes #3170\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
